**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/*.user
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Staging.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pfx
**/*.pem
**/*.key
# Keystores. This list never carried .p12 at all, and never .jks or .keystore either, though
# tools/status.sh names those last two as the SIGN-1 tripwire. The signing keystore lives
# off-tree so no build context ever held one, but the exclusion should not depend on that.
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.bks
# ASP.NET DataProtection key rings (2026-08-29 incident): AppKeys:KeyRingPath is the relative
# path "keys", so a ring minted by running the app from a clone sits beside the source and would
# otherwise ride into the build context. `**/*.key` above does NOT cover it -- a ring is an XML
# file named key-<guid>.xml. Both the ring directory and a loose ring file are excluded. Matches
# a path component named EXACTLY "keys", so the vendored wwwroot jquery.hotkeys/ tree is untouched.
**/keys/
**/key-*.xml
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
# Self-host packaging (OSS_NODE_PLAN 5/6.5): keep the root build context lean -- the node
# images restore/build from source only; tests, docs, and local run litter never ship.
tests/
docs/
**/logs/
